# PyJetra

A modern, bilingual (Sync and Async) Python wrapper for the Jetra Bot API.

[![PyPI](https://img.shields.io/badge/pypi-v1.6.0-blue?style=for-the-badge)](https://pypi.org/project/pyjetra/)
[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.7+-green?style=for-the-badge)](https://www.python.org/)
[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-orange?style=for-the-badge)](LICENSE)

## English

### What is PyJetra?

PyJetra is a Python library for building [Jetra](https://jetra.ir/) bots.
It provides a clean interface over the Jetra Bot API with full support
for both synchronous (requests) and asynchronous (aiohttp) workflows.

### Features

- Sync and Async clients: JetraBot (requests) and AsyncJetraBot (aiohttp)
- Full Bot API coverage: messages, media, edits, deletes, callbacks, webhooks
- Group management: ban, unban, restrict, permissions, leave, member info
- Chat member events: on_chat_member, on_my_chat_member
- FSM state management: set_state, get_state, clear_state
- Inline keyboards: multi-level menus, URL buttons, callbacks
- Advanced filters: CommandFilter, TextFilter, RegexFilter
- Ephemeral messages (Jetra-specific): edit and delete temporary messages
- Menu button and mini-app support
- Jetra-specific permissions: can_send_stickers, can_send_gifs
- Webhook ready: set_webhook, delete_webhook, get_webhook_info
- Rich Message and ChatMember types
- Type hints and clean dataclasses

### Installation

FENCEbash
pip install pyjetra
FENCE

### Quick start

FENCEpython
from pyjetra import JetraBot, CommandFilter, InlineKeyboardMarkup, InlineKeyboardButton

bot = JetraBot("YOUR_BOT_TOKEN")

@bot.on_message(filters=[CommandFilter("start")])
def start(msg):
    keyboard = InlineKeyboardMarkup([
        [InlineKeyboardButton(text="Open Jetra", url="https://jetra.ir")],
        [InlineKeyboardButton(text="About", callback_data="about")],
    ])
    msg.reply("Welcome to PyJetra!", reply_markup=keyboard)

@bot.on_callback_query()
def on_button(cb):
    if cb.data == "about":
        cb.answer("PyJetra v1.6.0")

bot.poll()
FENCE

### FSM example

FENCEpython
@bot.on_message(filters=[CommandFilter("register")])
def register(msg):
    bot.set_state(msg.from_user.id, "waiting_for_name")
    msg.reply("What's your name?")

@bot.on_message()
def handle_name(msg):
    if bot.get_state(msg.from_user.id) == "waiting_for_name":
        bot.clear_state(msg.from_user.id)
        msg.reply(f"Nice to meet you, {msg.text}!")
FENCE

### Group management example

FENCEpython
from pyjetra import ChatPermissions

@bot.on_message(filters=[CommandFilter("ban")])
def ban(msg):
    bot.ban_chat_member(-1001234567890, 12345)
    msg.reply("Banned.")

@bot.on_message(filters=[CommandFilter("mute")])
def mute(msg):
    perms = ChatPermissions(can_send_messages=False)
    bot.restrict_chat_member(-1001234567890, 12345, perms)
    msg.reply("Muted.")

@bot.on_my_chat_member()
def on_bot_status(event):
    print("Bot status:", event.new_chat_member.status)
FENCE

Note: chat_member and my_chat_member updates must be requested
explicitly:

FENCEpython
bot.poll(allowed_updates=[
    "message",
    "edited_message",
    "callback_query",
    "chat_member",
    "my_chat_member",
])
FENCE

### Async client

FENCEpython
import asyncio
from pyjetra import AsyncJetraBot, CommandFilter

bot = AsyncJetraBot("YOUR_BOT_TOKEN")

@bot.on_message(filters=[CommandFilter("start")])
async def start(msg):
    await bot.send_message(msg.chat.id, "Async works.")

asyncio.run(bot.start_polling())
FENCE

### Complete API reference

All 58 public methods below are available on both JetraBot and
AsyncJetraBot. The asynchronous versions must be awaited.

| Category | Method | Notes |
|----------|--------|-------|
| Account | get_me | Returns User. |
| Group | get_chat(chat_id) | Chat info dict. |
| Group | get_chat_member(chat_id, user_id) | Returns ChatMember. |
| Group | get_chat_administrators(chat_id, return_bots=False) | Returns list of ChatMember. |
| Group | get_chat_member_count(chat_id) | Integer. |
| Group | ban_chat_member(chat_id, user_id, until_date=None) | Optional temp ban. |
| Group | unban_chat_member(chat_id, user_id, only_if_banned=False) | |
| Group | restrict_chat_member(chat_id, user_id, permissions, ...) | permissions accepts ChatPermissions or dict. |
| Group | set_chat_permissions(chat_id, permissions, ...) | |
| Group | leave_chat(chat_id) | |
| Send | send_message(chat_id, text, ...) | |
| Send | send_rich_message(chat_id, text, ...) | Jetra-specific. |
| Send | send_photo(chat_id, photo_path, ...) | |
| Send | send_live_photo(chat_id, photo_path, ...) | Jetra-specific. |
| Send | send_document(chat_id, document_path, ...) | |
| Send | send_video(chat_id, video_path, ...) | |
| Send | send_video_note(chat_id, video_note_path, ...) | |
| Send | send_audio(chat_id, audio_path, ...) | |
| Send | send_voice(chat_id, voice_path, ...) | |
| Send | send_sticker(chat_id, sticker_path, ...) | |
| Send | send_animation(chat_id, animation_path, ...) | |
| Send | send_location(chat_id, latitude, longitude, ...) | |
| Send | send_contact(chat_id, phone_number, first_name, ...) | |
| Send | send_venue(chat_id, latitude, longitude, title, address, ...) | |
| Edit | edit_message_text(chat_id, message_id, text, ...) | |
| Edit | edit_message_caption(chat_id, message_id, caption, ...) | |
| Edit | edit_message_media(chat_id, message_id, media, ...) | |
| Edit | edit_message_reply_markup(chat_id, message_id, ...) | |
| Edit | delete_message(chat_id, message_id) | |
| Ephemeral | edit_ephemeral_message_text(chat_id, message_id, text, ...) | Jetra-specific. |
| Ephemeral | edit_ephemeral_message_caption(chat_id, message_id, caption, ...) | Jetra-specific. |
| Ephemeral | edit_ephemeral_message_media(chat_id, message_id, media, ...) | Jetra-specific. |
| Ephemeral | edit_ephemeral_message_reply_markup(chat_id, message_id, ...) | Jetra-specific. |
| Ephemeral | delete_ephemeral_message(chat_id, message_id) | Jetra-specific. |
| Files | get_file(file_id) | |
| Files | download_file(file_id, destination_path) | Returns local path. |
| Commands | set_my_commands(commands) | List of dicts. |
| Commands | get_my_commands() | |
| Commands | delete_my_commands() | |
| Webhook | set_webhook(url, secret_token=None, allowed_updates=None) | |
| Webhook | delete_webhook() | |
| Webhook | get_webhook_info() | |
| Menu | set_chat_menu_button(chat_id=None, menu_button=None) | Jetra-specific. |
| Menu | get_chat_menu_button(chat_id=None) | Jetra-specific. |
| Mini-app | set_user_emoji_status(user_id, ...) | Jetra-specific. |
| Mini-app | answer_web_app_query(web_app_query_id, result) | Jetra-specific. |
| Mini-app | save_prepared_inline_message(user_id, result, ...) | Jetra-specific. |
| Callback | answer_callback_query(callback_query_id, text=None, show_alert=False) | |
| Updates | get_updates(offset=0, allowed_updates=None) | |
| Events | on_message(func=None, filters=None) | Decorator. |
| Events | on_edited_message(func=None, filters=None) | Decorator. |
| Events | on_callback_query(func=None) | Decorator. |
| Events | on_chat_member(func=None) | Decorator. |
| Events | on_my_chat_member(func=None) | Decorator. |
| FSM | set_state(user_id, state) | |
| FSM | get_state(user_id) | |
| FSM | clear_state(user_id) | |
| Runner | poll(allowed_updates=None) / start_polling(...) | Sync / Async. |
| Runner | process_update(update) | Manual dispatch. |

### Types

- User, Chat, Message, CallbackQuery
- ChatMember, ChatMemberUpdated
- ChatPermissions (includes Jetra extensions can_send_stickers, can_send_gifs)
- InlineKeyboardMarkup, InlineKeyboardButton

### Filters

- CommandFilter("start") or CommandFilter(["start", "help"])
- TextFilter("exact text")
- RegexFilter(r"pattern")

### Errors

All API errors raise pyjetra.JetraError.

FENCEpython
from pyjetra import JetraError

try:
    bot.send_message(0, "test")
except JetraError as e:
    print("API error:", e)
FENCE

### Environment

Set PYJETRA_NO_BANNER=1 to suppress the startup banner.

